Privacy Policy
MySafeVid — VAA

Effective date: November 28, 2026

1. Personal information
MySafeVid is a free application developed by VAA to help parents manage approved video content. No account, name, telephone number or date of birth is required. We do not integrate our own advertising networks, behavioral tracking or analytics SDKs, sell personal information or use it for marketing. Technical information may be processed by necessary online services.

2. Local information
Approved channels and videos, titles, identifiers, thumbnail references, parental requests, language, protected PIN information and authentication tokens are stored on the device. Approval libraries are not synchronized to a central account. The PIN is not transmitted to our servers. Parental approvals are stored separately from temporary YouTube metadata. The Made for Kids setting and legal acceptance are also stored locally.

3. Permissions
The app does not require camera, microphone, contacts, precise location, personal files or photo gallery access. Internet access is necessary for browsing, metadata, security and playback.

4. YouTube services
We use YouTube API Services for public channel and video information and the official embedded player. No authorization of a personal Google account through the Data API is required. Google and YouTube may process IP addresses, device and browser information, cookies and interactions. YouTube controls advertisements, recommendations and links. See https://policies.google.com/privacy and https://www.youtube.com/t/terms MySafeVid is independent and is not endorsed by Google or YouTube.

5. Cloud infrastructure and security
Cloudflare provides the gateway and temporary caching. IP addresses, request details, timestamps and device or browser information may be processed for delivery, security and abuse prevention. Google Play Integrity verifies application authenticity. Integrity information and tokens are used for security, not advertising or profiling. See https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/ and https://policies.google.com/privacy.

6. Cookies
We do not use our own advertising or tracking cookies. YouTube browsing and playback may use cookies or similar storage for functionality, security, preferences and other purposes described in its privacy policy.

7. Children’s privacy
MySafeVid is intended for families, including children under parental or guardian supervision. Children are not required to provide directly identifying information. We do not use children’s personal information for personalized advertising or profiling. Parents should review this policy and supervise viewing. Approval does not guarantee suitability of content, advertisements or third-party interactions. Parents may contact us about their child’s information. Parents may restrict channel imports to videos designated Made for Kids by YouTube. This designation is not an independent safety assessment.

8. Retention and deletion
Parental preferences remain locally until removed or application data is cleared. Public API responses are cached in the cloud for up to 72 hours. Parents can remove approved items or clear application data in Android settings. This does not erase data independently held by third parties. Contact us to request access to or deletion of personal information, if any, held by VAA. Background maintenance attempts to refresh metadata from 25 days after retrieval and expires it at 30 days. Maintenance requires the app to be running and refresh requires connectivity. Expired metadata is excluded from viewing and cleaned up during maintenance; parental approvals are retained. Individually approved videos can recover automatically after a successful refresh. Channel collections may require a manual refresh.

9. Security
We use encrypted communications, protected PIN and token storage and integrity verification. No storage or transmission method guarantees absolute security.

10. External links
External services have their own terms and privacy practices, which VAA does not control. In Child mode, supported external navigation requests are subject to parental PIN authorization. The PIN is verified locally; authorization does not change the privacy practices of the destination.

11. Changes
Updated policies will be published with a revised effective date. Where necessary, users will be asked to review and accept them.

